  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In horizontal circle, tension towards the centre of the circular path at any moment will provide the required centripetal force.</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  }
